+    // moe-phone (patch 0013): CONFIDENCE GATES on what --predict-prefetch speculates. Measured on the
+    // 15R with 0012 (results/2026-09-18/specadopt_summary.json): selective adoption made 7.0 useful
+    // speculative experts/token and cut the stall 45 -> 36 ms, but read 130.7 vs 119.8 MiB/token,
+    // and not one refuted guess could be cancelled (every one had started reading by its layer's
+    // load). So the refuted bytes are paid at ISSUE time, and the only place to stop paying them is
+    // the issue decision. Both gates only remove experts from the speculation list; nothing that is
+    // computed changes (lossless, like the prefetch itself). Defaults keep 0012 behaviour exactly.
+    //   predict_spec_rank R  (0 = off): speculate a predicted miss only if its PREDICTED rank among
+    //                        the top-k is < R (rank 0 = the highest predicted score).
+    //   predict_spec_margin M (< 0 = off): speculate only if (score - boundary) / sd >= M, where
+    //                        boundary is the score of the first predicted expert OUTSIDE the top-k
+    //                        and sd the standard deviation of that layer's predicted scores over all
+    //                        experts. A small margin means the expert sits at the top-k edge, where
+    //                        the stale input is most likely to have reordered it.
+    int predict_spec_rank = 0;
+    float predict_spec_margin = -1.0f;
+
